# Raw inputs never move between laptops — outputs move instead (Master §7)
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
# ...except the labelled table that IS a deliverable. Repointed 13 Sept: the rule
# used to un-ignore features.csv, which is the OLD pre-clean-split file (trained and
# tested on Part III both). Un-ignoring it invited someone to commit it and quote
# numbers off a contaminated split, so it is ignored again on purpose.
# features_test.csv is the Part III HOLDOUT table -- 4,085 rows, 1.0 MB -- and it is
# the evidence behind every classical number we report. features_train.csv is 20 MB
# and stays out.
!data/labels/
data/labels/*
!data/labels/features_test.csv

# Environments
venv/
.venv/
.venv-api/
# Throwaway venv for OpenDrift (~90 packages incl. Cartopy). Deliberately NOT the project venv —
# see pipeline/drift/requirements-opendrift.txt for why it is installed separately.
odenv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Big raw formats — nothing over ~20 MB belongs in this repo
*.tif
*.tiff
# ...except the case bundle's 2-band SAR GeoTIFF: Stage 1 reads it from cases/<id>/ and the
# no-imports architecture needs it to travel with the repo (~8-10 MB/case at 10 m, tight box).
!cases/*/sar_vv_vh.tif
*.7z
*.zip
*.npz
*.parquet
*.pkl.gz

# Intermediate stage outputs — regenerable, the bundle in cases/ is the artefact
pipeline/*/out/
# NOT pipeline/*/results/. Those are the committed metric files — the evidence behind every
# number we quote — and the reasoning is the same one written under the model weights below:
# we ship CODE, not weights, so the training scripts and the eval JSONs ARE the reproducible
# artefact. out/ is scratch; results/ is evidence. Do not "tidy" results/ into this rule.

# Trained weights. GitHub hard-rejects any blob over 100 MB and models/ is 534 MB:
# classifier_vv_only.pkl is 204 MB and unet.pt / unet_baseline.pt are 121 MB each. We ship
# CODE, not weights — the training scripts and the eval JSONs are the reproducible artefact,
# and a 300-tree unbounded RandomForest is cheaper to retrain than to store. No LFS: the quota
# is shared, the objects outlive the repo, and nothing in the demo loads these files.
# NOTE (Soumirya, 13 Sept): these patterns must be **/models/*, not models/*. A gitignore pattern
# containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding the .gitignore, so "models/*" matches
# only a top-level models/ — which does not exist. The real path is pipeline/detect/models/, so
# the 534 MB stayed fully stageable and the push would have been rejected by GitHub.
**/models/*
!**/models/.gitkeep
# ...except the small ones the demo actually needs, and every metric file, which is evidence
# and must be in the repo whether or not the weights are (CLAUDE.md: "internals are binding").
!**/models/*.json
!**/models/scene_classifier.pt

# Throwaway end-to-end smoke / dry-run bundles (scripts/make_case000.py --scene-only)
cases/case-smoke/
cases/case-dry/

# Frontend build
web/.next/
web/dist/
web/public/cases/
# vendored maplibre worker + shared chunk, copied from node_modules by predev/prebuild
web/public/maplibre/

# Credentials — never, under any circumstances
.env
*.pem
.earthengine/
credentials.json

# Per-teammate handoff briefs — shared by hand (WhatsApp), never pushed
HANDOFF_*.md

# THE SEALED ANSWERS (Master Plan D21 / Part 16). Akshat holds this; nobody else sees it, and
# it must never reach a branch. docs/ANSWERS.README.md IS committed, so the team knows the
# file exists and who has it — hiding its existence would be worse than holding it.
docs/ANSWERS.md

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

Claude outputs/
